<title>USA: US attache shaves India 1997/98 wheat import forecast.</title>
<headline>US attache shaves India 1997/98 wheat import forecast.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>A U.S. agricultural attache shaved his forecast for India 1997/98 wheat imports by 500,000 tonnes to 3.0 million tonnes, due in part to the Indian government's recent move to partially liberalize rice imports.</p>
<p>&quot;A recent decision to allow rice imports could help ease some of the pressure on rice and wheat supplies,&quot; the attache wrote in a report dated June 2 released here Thursday.</p>
<p>&quot;However, imports are not expected in large quantities at this stage unless domestic prices move up significantly. Nevertheless, with 350,000 mt (tonnes) of rice imports forecast for 1997 and 1998, we reducing our 1997/98 wheat import forecast to 3.0 mmt (tonnes),&quot; the attache wrote.</p>
</text>
